{
  "_about": {
    "extension": "Official leaders: civilization.fandom.com/wiki/Leaders_(Civ6), read on 2026-09-28. A leader with no pack footnote and no R&F/GS icon in the main table is taken as base game. Persona pairs: the persona whose leader ability matches the main-table ability keeps the original leader's extension; the other persona gets the pack given in the 'Alternate personas' table (this pairing rule is an interpretation). BBG Expanded leaders: first BBG version whose bbg_expanded_X.html page lists them (github.com/civ6bbg/civ6bbg.github.io, commit d7119de).",
    "gender": "Wikidata property P21 (sex or gender) of the item linked from the leader's English Wikipedia article, the article itself being the first Wikipedia link on the leader's fandom page (official leaders) or chosen by name (BBG Expanded leaders). null = no P21 found.",
    "continent": "Official civs: 'Location' field of the civ infobox on civilization.fandom.com (text kept in 'location'). BBG Expanded civs: Wikidata P30 or Wikidata/Wikipedia description (text kept in 'location'). Mapping from the location text to continent labels is manual; entries marked interpretation=true are not a direct reading of the text.",
    "extensionOrder": "data/config.json extensionOrder (chronological order of the Extension column): PC release dates from civilization.fandom.com/wiki/DLC_(Civ6) (packs) and the infoboxes of Civilization_VI (2016-10-21), Civilization_VI:_Rise_and_Fall (2018-02-08), Civilization_VI:_Gathering_Storm (2019-02-14), read on 2026-09-29. Same-day releases share a rank (Ethiopia + both Persona Packs 2020-07-23; Great Negotiators + Julius Caesar 2022-11-21). BBG Expanded 7.1 and 7.5 are placed after all official packs (assumption, no date source) and 7.1 before 7.5 (version order)."
  },
